Audit: Agent

Purpose:
  Defines agent audit trail and traceability requirements.

AuditTrail:
  Every action MUST be recorded with:
    - Execution ID
    - Timestamp
    - Actor (agent/user)
    - Action type
    - Target
    - Risk level
    - Policy decision
    - Approval status
    - Result
    - Duration

Traceability:
  Every action MUST link to:
    - User request
    - Task
    - Workflow
    - Skill
    - Decision
    - Source
    - Test
    - Result

ExecutionID:
  Format:
    RUN-YYYYMMDD-NNN

  ActionID:
    RUN-YYYYMMDD-NNN/A01
    RUN-YYYYMMDD-NNN/A02

AgentResult:
  Format:
    TASK: TASK-<ID>

    Status:
      VERIFIED

    Changed:
      <N> files

    Tests:
      BDD PASS
      Unit PASS
      Integration PASS
      Security PASS

    Risk:
      Medium

    Remaining:
      None

SelfReview:
  Agent MUST analyze after each change:
    - What changed?
    - Why?
    - What could break?
    - What dependencies changed?
    - What tests cover it?
    - What security risks exist?

DiffReview:
  Reviewer sees:
    - Git diff
    - Impact graph
    - Tests
    - Security result

AuditRules:
  [AU1]  Every action MUST be auditable.
  [AU2]  Audit trail MUST include full traceability chain.
  [AU3]  Audit data MUST be immutable.
  [AU4]  Agent MUST provide concise summary to user, detailed logs to audit layer.
  [AU5]  Full prompt/history MUST NOT be stored (token/storage saving).

State: +
  
